  "answer_text": "**The comic came first!** Here's a quick breakdown:\n\n- **The Comic Book:** *The Walking Dead* is an American post-apocalyptic comic book series created by writer Robert Kirkman and artist Tony Moore. It began in **2003** and was published by Image Comics, running for 193 issues until Kirkman unexpectedly ended it in 2019.\n\n- **The TV Show:** AMC picked up the rights to make a series based on the comic in **2009**, ordered a pilot episode on January 21, 2010, with filming starting on May 15, 2010. The series premiered on **October 31, 2010**.\n\nSo the comic predates the TV show by **7 years**. The AMC television series (2010\u20132022) loosely follows the storyline of the comic book.",
